.TH AVR\-FEEDBACK 1 "" "avr 0.8.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-feedback \- Send feedback or report a bug.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr feedback
[OPTIONS] MESSAGE | status FEEDBACK_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send feedback or report a bug.
.PP
Send MESSAGE to the Avrea team. Sign in with avr auth login first.
.PP
Use --bug for a bug report and --org SLUG_OR_ID to attribute it to an organization. Without --org, feedback is personal, regardless of your default organization. Contact details come from your account.
.PP
The idempotency key is printed before sending. If the response is lost or the server asks you to retry, repeat the same message, --bug setting and organization with --idempotency-key KEY. For a key conflict, use the original content or omit --idempotency-key to create a new submission. Acceptance queues delivery; use avr feedback status FEEDBACK_ID to check it. Use -- before a message beginning with a dash, help, or a word resembling status.
.PP
Examples: avr feedback "Please support Lambda Cloud" avr feedback --bug "Run logs are missing" avr feedback status FEEDBACK_ID
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
[\fIMESSAGE\fR]
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bug\fR
Mark the feedback as a bug report.
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fITEXT\fR
Reuse a previous submission UUID (normalized to 32 lowercase hex characters).
.TP
\fB\-\-jq\fR, \fB\-q\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter JSON with an embedded jq expression.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output comma-separated fields, * for all, or ? to list fields.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Attribute feedback to this organization slug or ID.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
status
Read the delivery status of your feedback.
